menu "M5CoreAnalyser BSP (M5Stack Core2) Configuration"

    config BSP_ADC1_QEMU_MIDSCALE_FALLBACK
        bool "Test-only: return mid-scale (2048) from bsp_adc1_read_raw() instead of hardware ADC reads"
        default n
        help
            The ESP32 QEMU machine does not emulate the SAR ADC (SENS) registers, so
            adc_oneshot_read() spins forever there. Enable this ONLY in test/QEMU builds
            (test_app/sdkconfig.defaults). When enabled, bsp_adc1_read_raw() always returns
            2048 without touching hardware and bsp_adc1_uses_mock_fallback() returns true.
            Production firmware keeps this disabled so every ADC read uses adc_oneshot_read()
            and failures are propagated to the caller, never silently replaced with mid-scale.

endmenu
